      <span>•</span>
      <span>SMACNA &amp; IRC Section R905.10</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
      Metal Roof Valley Flashing: Open vs Closed W-Valley Details
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Roof valleys carry the highest volume and velocity of rainwater on any structure. On metal roofs, standard V-shaped valleys fail during torrential downpours because water rushing down one slope shoots directly up underneath the opposite panels! Here is how to install an engineered W-profile open valley with continuous water diverters.
    </p>

    <!-- Quick Stats Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Minimum Metal Width</div>
        <div class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900 mt-0.5">20" to 24" (10"-12" per side)</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Splash Diverter Height</div>
        <div class="text-sm font-bold text-emerald-600 mt-0.5">1-inch Center "W" Rib</div>
      </div>
      <div>
